WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.087
The core object is a basis for equivariant graph
polynomials.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:08.733
Each basis element is a directed multi-graph with a
marked red edge,

00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:11.329
and its value is a tensor contraction,

00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:15.633
an einsum over adjacency entries that sums over
internal nodes.

00:00:15.713 --> 00:00:20.415
Averaging monomials over all node permutations, the
Reynolds operator,

00:00:20.495 --> 00:00:21.986
makes them equivariant.

00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:23.421
To analyze a network,

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:29.501
the authors treat it as a bank of primitive
contractions and give a linear-time algorithm

00:00:29.581 --> 00:00:32.438
deciding which polynomials it can assemble.

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:37.904
Node-based banks equal one-WL, edge-based banks
equal two-FWL, that is three-WL.

00:00:37.984 --> 00:00:42.959
Building on this, PPGN plus plus feeds in
precomputed polynomial features,

00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:45.350
lifting it strictly above three-WL.
